/* wardrobe.dat.js: DATA for the three walk-in wardrobes of the attic and the niche of room 6 (numbers and descriptions only, no calculations): the design
   written part by part, drawn and listed as it is. Every length is in mm, house axes (x along the house, y across, z up).

   The rooms are the house's (through the interface ../../shell.js): walls, floor, ceiling, the roof and the door are taken from
   there and not repeated here. A wardrobe is the house's room of that number.

   wardrobes   by the room's number: name; cameras (the dock); carcasses (what Info lists of each: its run, its span along the wall
               [y1, y2], width, depth, height, its top, the fixed and movable shelves and the drawers); movers (a drawer: the
               solids with its id slide by [dx, dy] when it opens); solids, board by board:
                 name     the carcass (or the run, for a plinth)
                 label    what the part is (the cutting list's name)
                 layer    of views.3d.layers
                 material a key of looks
                 box      [x1, x2, y1, y2, z1, z2]
                 board    a key of boards: what it is cut from; cut [a, b, edges along a, edges along b] as the cutting list gives it
                 mover    the drawer it belongs to
   boards      the board of each kind of part (keys of ../../library/products boards)
   looks       the material of each kind of part (keys of ../../library/materials.dat.js)
   estimate    Info's Kosztorys: the sheet (mm), the waste on the boards; what is bought (keys of the library) by what is counted
               in the solids: per (a label, a mover, a carcass, a movable shelf) × each, in packs of pack; or by measure
               (edges: the banded edges in m, cuts: the cuts in m, length of a label: its solids' length in m) */
